# SwarmForge Constitution

## Purpose
This document defines the rules, roles, and workflows governing SwarmForge. All agents must obey these instructions when contributing to the project.

## Structure
The constitution lives in numbered **articles** under
`swarmforge/constitution/articles/`: 1 Roles and Responsibilities, 2 Handoff
Protocol, 3 Backlog Management, 4 Quality Gates, 5 Amendments. The directory
also carries unnumbered project-wide prompt articles (`engineering.prompt`,
`workflow.prompt`, `local-engineering.prompt`, `project.prompt`). Long-form
incident-backed elaborations live under `.../articles/reference/` (e.g.
`engineering-detailed.prompt`) — **not** inlined at boot, read on demand. See
**reference/constitution-prompt-detailed.md** for this section's pre-trim wording.

## Key Rules
The four load-bearing rules below are stated in full in their own articles
(inlined right after this file, same boot prefix) — restated here only as an
index, not duplicated at length: **Pipeline Flow** (the `specifier → coder →
cleaner → architect → hardender → documenter → QA (integrate) → coordinator
(bookkeep)` chain — `PIPELINE.md`), **Worktrees** (per-role in `01_roles.md`,
the full table in `PIPELINE.md`), **Handoffs** (Article 2.3, `02_handoffs.md`),
and the **No-Op Rule** (Article 1.9 / 2.3.2). See
**reference/constitution-prompt-detailed.md** for this section's pre-trim wording.

## Amendments
To propose a change to the constitution, see Article 5 (`05_amendments.md`)
— the process is defined there once, in full, not repeated here.
